        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r209249704-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Closed, but...",
        "text": "The temple itself is not open to non-Hindus and is protected by high walls, but its setting on the sacred Bagmati River and the complex of minor temples, bathing ghats and crematory sites in its grounds make this an extraordinary place to visit. The final stages of the Hindu cremation take place in the open air on the river bank, from anointing the body, to setting the pyre alight, to cremation, to shovelling the ashes into the river and preparing a new funeral pyre.\nA home for the elderly sits adjacent to the crematorium with a huge, shifting pile of firewood outside. One wonders what the residents must think, being within sight, sound and smell of their eventual departure from this world?",
