        "title": "Not for the squeamish but a good cultural learning experience",
        "text": "This is a very important Hindu temple and crematorium. I would recommend that you acquire a guide unless you are already knowledgeable about this process. The small river actually is a tributary of the Ganges, important for Hindus. There will likely be bodies burning on the stands above the river but they are covered up - it is OK. You can not enter the temple area but are able to stand across the river from it and the ceremonial cremations. Walk up the hill behind you for a stunning hilltop view.",
